pgpdump
------------------------------------------
pgpdump is a PGP packet visualizer which displays the packet format of OpenPGP
(RFC 4880) and PGP version 2 (RFC 1991).

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libbz2_1-1.0.8-2
  zlib0-1.3.2-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libbz2-devel-1.0.8-2
  make-4.4.1-2
  zlib-devel-1.3.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/kazu-yamamoto/pgpdump/

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/kazu-yamamoto/pgpdump/archive/refs/tags/v0.38.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack pgpdump-0.38-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./pgpdump-0.38-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/pgpdump-0.38-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/pgpdump-0.38-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(pgpdump)
  /usr/bin/pgpdump.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/pgpdump.README
  /usr/share/doc/pgpdump/COPYRIGHT
  /usr/share/doc/pgpdump/ChangeLog.md
  /usr/share/doc/pgpdump/README.md
  /usr/share/man/man1/pgpdump.1.gz

